# Copy, don't mutate

Prefer immutable structs and containers. Copy data; do not write through arguments (pointer targets, slice elements, map entries).

Methods may mutate the receiver. Assigning into a local slice or map the function allocated is fine. Rebinding a parameter is fine.

Do not import third-party immutable collection libraries. Overkill. Use stdlib slices, maps, and structs.

Do not be fanatic. If a mutating API is clearly simpler and you are unsure, ask the user.

```go
// BAD
func enrich(videos []LikedVideo) { videos[0].Duration = d }
func apply(v *LikedVideo, d details) { v.Duration = d.Duration }

// GOOD
func merge(v LikedVideo, d details) LikedVideo {
	v.Duration = d.Duration
	return v
}

videos[i] = merge(videos[i], d) // local slice the function allocated
```
